WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.840
The bottled water can sell for 100 times what the water and the plastic actually cost. This

00:00:05.840 --> 00:00:12.000
is First Principles Daily, episode 76. A half liter bottle of water at a gas station

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.700
cooler commonly sells for something like a dollar and a half. Sometimes more, wave a magic

00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:23.820
wand and arrange the raw atoms, municipal water, a dozen grams of polyethylene tariff thalate,

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:30.380
or PET, and a polypropylene cap, and the materials inside that bottle are worth a couple of

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:36.740
cents. The liquid is not scarce, the polymer is not scarce. What you are buying is a sealed,

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:43.060
branded, refrigerated object that has been driven across a landscape already plumbed with safe water.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:49.440
The gap between those two cents and that dollar and a half is the entire industry. Bottled water

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:56.000
did not start as a way to move municipal supply in disposable plastic. The 19th and 20th century

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:03.600
European Springs, Evian, Perrier, San Pellegrino sold mineral content, a place, and a status object,

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.440
often in glass, to people who already had water at home. That luxury template was still visible when

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:18.180
the American market exploded in the 1970s and 1980s. Then the category flipped. In the 1990s, the

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.600
big beverage companies walked in with a different product. City water run through carbon filters,

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:31.860
reverse osmosis, and ultraviolet or ozone poured into PET and named. Aquafina and Dessani are the

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:37.840
famous cases, and they are not unique. A large share of the purified water on North American shelves

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:44.940
is municipal supply with a treatment step and a label. The industry learned that you do not need a

00:01:44.940 --> 00:01:51.520
plant, a bottle, a truck, and a story about purity. Once that template existed, every incentive and

00:01:51.520 --> 00:01:57.280
consumer packaged goods piled onto it. Beverage companies already had filling lines, cold drink

00:01:57.280 --> 00:02:02.940
distribution, and supermarket relationships. Water was a volume stockkeeping unit that did not

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:09.660
compete with their own soda as harshly as a rival cola would, and it rode the same trucks. Retailers

00:02:09.660 --> 00:02:15.420
learned that water is an impulse item with reliable turns, especially at convenience and in the checkout

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:22.620
cooler. Brands learned that mountain photography and words like Alpine, Artesian, and Pure sell even

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:29.100
when the intake pipe is in the same town as the customer. Advertising, slotting fees, and trade spend

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:35.100
accreted on top of manufacturing the way they do on every other branded grocery product. None of

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:41.440
this required a conspiracy. It required the ordinary machinery of consumer packaged goods applied to

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:47.080
a liquid that costs almost nothing. The price then feels normal because the object in your hand is

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:53.100
no longer water. It is a cold, sealed, portable serving with a trusted name sitting where you

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:59.460
already stopped for fuel. Tap water requires a glass, a fountain that works, and a belief that the pipe

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:05.360
is safe. In cities that have had lead, boil water notices, or simply old buildings with ugly

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:11.880
fountains, that belief is not free. Airports, stadiums, and offices stripped out fountains or let them

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:18.760
decay, then rented coolers and sold cases. Parents packed bottles into lunch bags until the next generation

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:25.200
treated the single serve PET as the default unit of hydration. By the time Americans were drinking

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:31.460
more bottled water than soda, tens of gallons per person per year in the commonly reported tallies,

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:37.420
the category no longer had to justify itself against the tap. It only had to justify itself

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:43.000
against the other bottles on the same shelf. Regulation quietly helped the feeling of specialness.

00:03:43.460 --> 00:03:49.240
In the United States, tap water is an environmental protection agency matter and bottled water is a

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.960
food and drug administration food. The two regimes test for overlapping but not identical things

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:00.900
on different schedules with different public reporting. That split is often sold implicitly

00:04:00.900 --> 00:04:06.560
as the bottle being more tightly controlled. It is not a reliable safety ranking. It is a

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:12.240
jurisdictional accident that marketing was happy to wear. Add the fact that chlorine in city water

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:18.640
is noticeable and reverse osmosis filtrate tastes clean and you have a sensory alibi for a thousand

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:25.280
percent markup. Inside the industry, a dollar for a half liter is not a scandal. It is the working

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:31.800
retail price of a convenience beverage and convenience beverages are supposed to be expensive. So take the

00:04:31.800 --> 00:04:37.340
object apart and price the atoms. Start with the actual materials in the most common serving,

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:44.060
a half liter single serve bottle. The water is 500 milliliters of something a city already treated

00:04:44.060 --> 00:04:50.560
and piped. Residential volumetric water charges in much of North America, once you stop mixing them

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:56.880
with sewer and fixed meter fees, often land around a few dollars per thousand gallons. A thousand

00:04:56.880 --> 00:05:05.000
gallons is 3,785 liters. A few dollars spread over that volume is a small fraction of a cent per liter,

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:11.120
commonly in the neighborhood of a tenth of a cent, sometimes less, sometimes a few tenths depending

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:18.180
on the utility. Half a liter is then a few hundreds of a cent. It is fair to call the water as a commodity

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:25.700
rounding error. Purifying it again does not rescue the price. Reverse osmosis at industrial scale is an

00:05:25.700 --> 00:05:31.720
energy and membrane problem. Efficient systems often use something like one to a few kilowatt hours

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:38.020
per cubic meter, which is a thousandths of a kilowatt hour per liter or a little more. At ordinary

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:44.460
industrial electricity prices, that is another tiny fraction of a cent. Carbon, ultraviolet lamps

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:50.860
and ozone at the throughput of a bottling plant are not free, but they do not add sense per liter either.

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:57.880
They add fractions. The magic wand water plus treatment number, the cost of arranging H2O

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:03.800
into a drinkable, low total dissolved solids liquid, is still a fraction of a cent per half liter

00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:10.400
Anyone who has run a home under sink reverse osmosis system and divided the filter and electricity

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:16.780
bill by the leaders produced has seen a version of the same arithmetic. The bottle is the first material

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:23.660
that actually shows up. Bottle grade PET resin is a commodity that moves with oil and perexiling.

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:29.500
Across recent years it has typically traded in a band around one to two dollars per kilogram,

00:06:30.060 --> 00:06:35.980
sometimes spiking outside that band, often sitting inside it. Years of light weighting have

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:42.440
brought many half liter bottles down to roughly 8 to 12 grams for the body. 10 grams is a hundredth

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:49.600
of a kilogram. At a dollar 50 a kilo, that body is about a cent and a half of polymer. Use 12 grams

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:55.740
and two dollars a kilo and you are still around two and a half cents of PET. The cap is a couple of

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:01.320
grams of polypropylene or high density polyethylene. Another few tenths of a cent of resin.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:07.780
The label is a sliver of filament ink, glue, ink and the dust of process chemicals do not change

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:15.440
the column. Add it up out loud, water and retreatment negligible. PET body about one and a half to two

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:22.660
and a half cents, cap a few tenths, label rounding error. A rough magic wand estimate for the finished

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:28.120
half liter object is two to four cents of raw material and it is honest to lean toward the

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:34.000
low end of that range for a modern lightweight bottle at ordinary resin prices. A one liter bottle

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:40.280
uses more polymer, often something like 20 grams give or take after light weighting, so the floor

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:47.420
rises but it rises into the low single cents not into the dollars. Now the idiot index kept visible

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:53.260
as arithmetic rather than as a fact of nature. Take two and a half cents as a generous material floor

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:59.720
for the half liter. A warehouse club case can put that same bottle on a pantry shelf for roughly 15 to

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:06.600
25 cents. Divide 20 cents by two and a half cents and you get a ratio around eight. That is already

00:08:06.600 --> 00:08:12.920
a loud number for a product whose physics are this simple but it is the cheap end. Grocery singles

00:08:12.920 --> 00:08:18.820
sit higher. A convenience store or airport cooler commonly asks a dollar and a half to two and a half

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:25.140
dollars for the identical 500 milliliters. A dollar 50 divided by two and a half cents is 60.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:31.200
Two dollars divided by two cents is a hundred. Premium spring and imported still waters,

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:37.260
the Fiji and Evion shelf, can sit at two to four dollars a liter which is a still larger multiple,

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:41.980
though those at least sometimes contain dissolved minerals you cannot get from the kitchen tap.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:48.460
None of these ratios is a laboratory measurement of anyone's cost of goods. They are a back of the

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:54.540
envelope comparison of public retail prices to public commodity prices and they are enough to show the

00:08:54.540 --> 00:09:00.820
shape of the opportunity. Even the cheap case of bottled water is several times the atoms. The bottle

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:06.760
you actually grab when you are thirsty is tens of times the atoms, sometimes a hundred. Where does a

00:09:06.760 --> 00:09:13.500
factor of 60 live if it does not live in the PET? Walk the chain. Pellets become preforms become

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:19.420
stretch blown bottles. That conversion is one of the most optimized pieces of plastics processing on

00:09:19.420 --> 00:09:26.000
earth. High speed blow molders do not turn two cents of resin into a 50 cent empty bottle. They turn

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:33.180
it into an empty bottle that still costs sense. Energy, machine time, scrap, labor, the mold, a small

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:39.220
multiple of the resin, not two orders of magnitude. Filling, capping and labeling on a rotary line that

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:44.960
runs hundreds of bottles a minute likewise cannot explain a dollar. Capital equipment is expensive,

00:09:45.340 --> 00:09:51.420
but it is amortized over enormous counts. The labor and utilities per unit at a modern plant are small.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:58.300
Secondary packaging, the shrink wrap, the corrugated tray, the palette, adds more sense. You can

00:09:58.300 --> 00:10:04.560
spend a generous 10 or 15 cents of conversion, fill, pack, and plant overhead, and still not have

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:10.460
accounted for the convenience store price. The materials plus plant story pops out well before the

00:10:10.460 --> 00:10:17.580
register. The rest is movement, rent, and narrative. Waterways one kilogram per liter. A trailer that

00:10:17.580 --> 00:10:23.540
can legally haul about 20 tons is hauling about 20,000 liters if it is full of filled bottles.

00:10:23.540 --> 00:10:30.040
And a non-trivial share of that mass is PET and corrugated rather than water. Diesel,

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:35.980
driver, tractor, insurance, and the empty backhaul are being spent to relocate a liquid that the

00:10:35.980 --> 00:10:42.660
destination city already has in its mains. Regional distribution might add sense per bottle rather

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:47.860
than dollars. Exact freight allocations are not public and very wildly with distance,

00:10:47.860 --> 00:10:54.240
but the direction is insane in principle. The industry's core logistics task is to move water to

00:10:54.240 --> 00:11:00.080
places that have water. Then a distributor takes a margin. Then a retailer takes a larger one.

00:11:00.740 --> 00:11:05.340
Convenience retail in particular prices to the thirsty person standing in front of a cooler,

00:11:05.880 --> 00:11:11.840
not to the cost stack. The facing in the vault is expensive floor space. The refrigeration is a

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:17.400
real electricity bill and the category can bear a high markup because the comparison set is other

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:23.840
cold drinks, not the tap in the bathroom. Brand advertising and trade spend sit on top of that.

00:11:24.420 --> 00:11:30.000
A national water brand is buying the feeling that this particular municipal filtrate is the safe one

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:36.400
and that feeling is not a polymer. For the premium tier, add the photography of islands and alps,

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:42.100
the glass bottle cousin on the restaurant list, and the permission to charge a beverage price for a water

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:48.700
price. There is a genuine remainder that is not waste in the insulting sense. Sealed, portable, cold,

00:11:48.940 --> 00:11:54.760
and trustworthy is a product. A traveler at a gate, a crew on a job site without potable hose,

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.540
a household under a boil water notice, a parent who does not want to wash a bottle at a park.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:06.360
Those are real jobs to be done. The idiot index does not say those jobs are imaginary.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:12.260
It says that for the majority of leaders sold into kitchens, offices, and gym bags in cities with

00:12:12.260 --> 00:12:17.500
functioning utilities, the jobs are being done with a cost structure built for a luxury import,

00:12:18.080 --> 00:12:23.400
and the physics of the liquid do not require it. The arithmetic shows the gap lives in movement and

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:29.180
story, not atoms. A from scratch redesign does not begin with a slightly lighter bottle.

00:12:29.640 --> 00:12:35.840
It begins by refusing to long haul a ubiquitous liquid. The first move is to purify at the point of

00:12:35.840 --> 00:12:40.500
use or the point of sale, and to sell the treatment and the vessel, not the kilometers.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:46.120
Home picture filters and under sink reverse osmosis units already do a version of this.

00:12:46.840 --> 00:12:52.300
Amortized over their rated leaders, they produce drinking water at a tiny multiple of municipal rates,

00:12:52.720 --> 00:12:57.860
with the idiot index crushed because the trucking, the brand, and the single use conversion have been

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:03.140
deleted. What has to be true for that to take the rest of the market is boring and physical.

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:09.180
Filters that are cheap and easy to replace, membranes that last, and a public record of tap

00:13:09.180 --> 00:13:14.400
quality that people can believe without a mountain on the label. Utilities that publish live,

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:19.940
readable test data, and buildings that do not leach lead between the meter and the kitchen are not

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:26.020
marketing. They are the enabling infrastructure. The second move is refill as the default public

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:32.380
interface. That means fountains that are cold, fast, and obviously clean, not the warm dribble that

00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:37.540
taught a generation to walk to the cooler. And it means bottle filling stations in the same places

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:44.080
the industry currently owns, gyms, schools, airports, offices, parks, convenience store, four courts.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:50.740
Some of those stations already exist. The first principles version treats them as the primary product,

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:57.760
not as a sustainability afterthought next to a wall of PET. For this to work at scale, the empty

00:13:57.760 --> 00:14:03.540
vessel has to already be in the bag, which is a design problem. A bottle people actually carry,

00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:09.880
and a habit problem, not a chemistry problem. Deposit return and refill pricing that makes the

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:15.600
packaged leader look as expensive as it is would help. And several jurisdictions have already started

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:25.000
down that road with plastic taxes and deposits. The saving is almost the entire gap. You keep the

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:31.040
city freight, the single use conversion, and most of the brand. The third move is what remains of true

00:14:31.040 --> 00:14:38.560
single serve. Emergency supply, disaster staging, true mobile work, and the last mile of convenience will

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:44.920
still want a sealed unit. First principles would fill that unit locally from the same municipal source,

00:14:45.320 --> 00:14:51.180
in the lightest competent package, with no pretense of a distant spring, and would price it near

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:57.460
conversion plus logistics instead of near soda. A grocery chain already running a pharmacy and a

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:03.760
kitchen could run a reverse osmosis skid, and a small blow fill line in the back of the store. Or,

00:15:04.040 --> 00:15:11.320
simpler, a staffed or automated refill of a standardized deposit bearing bottle. What has to be true is

00:15:11.320 --> 00:15:17.380
local code that allows it. A quality system as boring as a dairies and a willingness to sell water

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:23.020
as water. The dollars that fall out are the national trucking network and the advertising budget.

00:15:23.580 --> 00:15:28.520
The hard parts are not the membranes. Trust is hard in cities that have earned distrust,

00:15:29.080 --> 00:15:35.340
and no amount of clever packaging should paper overled services or failed plants. Those are first

00:15:35.340 --> 00:15:41.800
principles water problems of a different kind, and bottled PET is a costly, regressive patch on them.

00:15:42.640 --> 00:15:47.680
Convenience at 2 in the morning in a place with no fountain is hard, and pretending it is not a

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:54.500
product is how refill schemes fail. Taste is hard in the small sense that declorinated reverse osmosis

00:15:54.500 --> 00:16:00.500
water and chlorinated tap are different, and people are allowed to prefer the former, which is an

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:06.300
argument for cheap local treatment, not for a brand from another watershed. The incumbent cooler

00:16:06.300 --> 00:16:12.000
footprint is hard because it is already paid for and it prints money. Premium mineral water is

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:17.800
a different object again. If you want the ions from a specific spring, you are not in the municipal

00:16:17.800 --> 00:16:23.080
filtrate business, and that slice of the shelf can stay expensive without confusing the rest.

00:16:23.720 --> 00:16:29.740
And the environmental accounting is not free even after the idiot index falls. PET, collection,

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:35.560
and recycling have their own physics, which is why the better redesign is fewer single use units,

00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:40.520
not merely cheaper ones. If a city already delivers the molecule to the building,

00:16:40.960 --> 00:16:46.240
a company that still makes its margin by putting that molecule on a truck is not selling hydration.

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:52.740
It is selling distance, refrigeration, and reassurance, and those should be priced and designed as

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:59.400
themselves. The second principle is older than PET. Do not run a logistics network whose payload

00:16:59.400 --> 00:17:04.900
exists at both ends of the route. The ice trade collapsed when we learned to make cold locally.

00:17:05.560 --> 00:17:09.760
Bottled municipal water is the same cargo, still waiting on the same realization.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:17.340
Who prices a liter of purified city water against the sense it contains? A utility, a grosser with a

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:24.060
reverse osmosis skid, a refill network, and what is the first stock keeping unit that admits on the label

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:28.960
that the spring is the mains? That's a wrap on today's first principles breakdown.

00:17:29.440 --> 00:17:35.560
The ideas travel further when you pass them on. Send this to a fellow builder. I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

